      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofdanville.org/1337/Historic-District",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1781–82 smallpox outbreak in Danville, then called Hawke, was one of the town’s most tragic events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danville%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Families first settled in the area around 1735, long before Danville’s official incorporation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danville%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "From 1790 onward, Danville invested heavily in road construction, turning its once footpath network into a more reliable thoroughfare.",
